  "categoryName": "Causalidad y daño",
  "motif": "Alcance del daño",
  "treatment": "mechanism",
  "family": "spatial-mechanism",
  "description": "An assembled fictional plate (Event A with its supplied consequences and two rings) comes apart into its pieces: the inner piece (the event, the ● ring and the consequences supplied as immediate) and the outer piece (the annulus, the ◆ ring and the consequences supplied as subsequent, to be examined), at equal size and weight on equal plinths, and the boundary piece — a radial cross-section through both rings, lifted out and enlarged. Only the supplied relationships are drawn with their kind (plain relation by default; causal only when supplied); a tracer follows the traversal order while the focus element enlarges. The rings are only a supplied grouping; nothing is tested, valued or decided.",
